SUMMARY:AI for Business: Hands-On Workshop
DESCRIPTION:AVL Digital Nomads\n**AI for Business: Hands-On Workshop**\n\\
 *\\*\\*Bring your laptop + a paid Anthropic/OpenAI account\\*\\*\\*\n**Spe
 aker:** [Julio Barros](https://www.linkedin.com/in/juliobarros)\n\n**Descr
 iption:**\nMost business owners have typed a question into ChatGPT. Far fe
 wer have given AI an actual job in their business. The gap between “aski
 ng AI questions” and “giving AI a job” is the biggest competitive wi
 ndow most of us will see.\n\nIn one evening we go from “what is Claude
 ” to a real working setup on your own laptop: a project the AI can see\,
  your business profile loaded into its memory\, one connector live (Gmail\
 , Calendar\, Notion\, whichever you use most)\, and a real task from your 
 week shipped. The task can be a recurring follow-up email\, a messy folder
  of receipts\, a report you rebuild every week\, etc. Anything you’d han
 d off if you had a junior assistant.\n\nWe’ll cover the same chatbot-to-
 co-worker progression I walk through in my talks\, but instead of watching
  me demo it\, you’ll work on something important to you.\n\nWhat to brin
 g:\n\\* a paid Anthropic or OpenAI account ($20 is fine)\n\\* a laptop\n\\
 * one tedious task you keep redoing\n\nBy the end of the session you’ll 
 have a working project\, at least one skill or scheduled task running\, an
 d a short list of what to automate next\, in what order\, so you don’t a
 utomate the wrong thing first.\n\nWho it’s for: business owners\, operat
 ors\, and team leads ready to move past “I tried ChatGPT once” and sta
 rt handing real work off.\n\n**General Event Info**\nAI Hacks and Hops is 
 a monthly event tailored for non-technical professionals\, entrepreneurs\,
  marketers\, engineers\, or anyone who wants to explore and discuss how to
  use AI.\n\nEach gathering will feature presentations\, stimulating group 
 discussions\, and a relaxed atmosphere for enjoying your favorite brews wh
 ile delving into the world of AI. Topics will range from AI integration in
  business processes\, marketing\, content creation\, software\, ethical co
 nsiderations\, human-AI collaboration strategies\, to the latest advanceme
 nts in AI technology. The informal setting encourages open dialogue\, idea
  exchange\, and fosters a collaborative spirit.
